{"id":"st2016-3","designation":"ST 2016-3","title":"Active Format Description — Vertical Ancillary Data Mapping of Active Format Description and Bar Data","state":"stabilized","suite":"2016","official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st2016-3/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st2016-3/","checked_at":"2026-11-18"},"scope":"This Standard defines a method of coding that allows Active Format Description (AFD) and Bar Data information to be carried in the 10-bit vertical ancillary (VANC) data space of a standard definition or high definition component television signal. The standard defines how the AFD and Bar Data information is placed into an AFD/Bar Data ancillary data packet for carriage in accordance with SMPTE 291M. An associated standard, SMPTE ST 2016-1, defines the format for AFD and Bar Data and identifies the video image and interface standards with which it may be associated. Annex C shows the relationship among the standards.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"SMPTE ST 2016-3:2009","page":1},{"level":1,"title":"Revision of SMPTE 2016-3-2007","page":1},{"level":1,"title":"Foreword","page":2},{"level":1,"title":"Intellectual Property","page":2},{"level":1,"title":"Introduction","page":2},{"level":1,"title":"1 Scope","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"2 Conformance Notation","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"3 Normative References","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"4 Format of VANC Data Packets","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"5 Location of the Vertical Ancillary Data","page":5},{"level":1,"title":"Annex A (Informative)","page":6},{"level":1,"title":"Bibliography","page":6},{"level":1,"title":"Annex B (Informative)","page":7},{"level":1,"title":"Comments on the Preferred Location of VANC Packets","page":7},{"level":1,"title":"Annex C (Informative)","page":8},{"level":1,"title":"Road Map to Related Standards for AFD, Bar Data, and Pan-Scan","page":8},{"level":1,"title":"Revision Notes","page":9}],"definitions":[],"keywords":[{"term":"Ancillary Data","zh":"辅助数据